  "formal_commutator_shift_reduction": "For EVERY commutative Q-algebra,arbitrary formal constant-coefficient T=lambda(partial),polynomial Q of degree delta and m>=delta,the finite commutator identity T^m M_Q=sum_(j<=delta)binom(m,j)(adT)^j(M_Q)T^(m-j) holds because adT lowers polynomial coefficient degree and adT^(delta+1)M_Q0. Hence T^(m-delta)f0 implies T^m(Qf)0. No finite differential order or zero constant symbol is required. Consequently separate eventuality for EVERY polynomial marker is EQUIVALENT to,for EVERY fixed shift d>=0,eventual vanishing T^k P^(k+d)0. On the pure locus d0 is already automatic. Every shift keeps its own eventual threshold;no one-shift theorem or linear bound is inferred. This extends deBondt1206.2836v2 Theorem1/Corollary2 by a direct formal normal-order proof and applies over nonreduced rings.",
  "actual_apolar_gap_equivalence": "For EVERY characteristic-zero FIELD,NONZERO polynomial P and arbitrary pure formal symbol,lambda(0)0 and h_m=max{k>=0:T^k P^m!=0} is finite. Let b_m=m-h_m,so purity gives1<=b_m<=m. In the ACTUAL local Artin apolar algebra A_m=K[[Z]]/Ann(P^m),h_m+1 is the nilpotence index of lambda. All individual markers are eventual iff b_m tends to infinity. One common linear cutoff exists iff epsilon=inf_m b_m/m>0,iff liminf_m b_m/m>0. If epsilon>0,ceil(1/epsilon) suffices by the formal commutator lemma. Conversely any valid cutoff C and degree bound D>=1 imply h_m<=CD*b_m and b_m/m>=1/(CD+1) for EVERY m,using the nonzero marker P^(m-h_m) at moment index h_m. Each height uses only the symbol jet through Dm;formal unit factors preserve every height. Thus the ENTIRE remaining OP-GVC-FORMAL-LINEAR is exactly the actual power-apolar gap question:b_m->infinity implies positive asymptotic fraction? This implication is NOT proved or refuted. Arbitrary abstract sequences are not actual realizations;no rational limit,linear eventual formula or additivity is claimed.",
  "ordinary_excess_power_cofinality": "In the universal polynomial coefficient ring for phase degree<=D>=1 and infinitely many formal symbol coefficients,let I_C be the ORDINARY ideal of all output coefficients T^m(x^alpha P^m) for m>Cabsalpha. Let E_N be the ORDINARY ideal of coefficients T^k P^(k+d) with d>=0,k>=1,k>Nd. For integers N,C>=0,one has I_(N+1) subset E_N and E_(CD) subset I_C,hence I_(CD+1) subset E_(CD) subset I_C. The first follows by applying the all-ring formal commutator lemma in the ACTUAL quotient by E_N at k=m-delta;the second expands P^d as a marker of degree<=Dd. All nilpotents/embedded structure are retained;no radical substitution,Noetherianity or infinite-ring ACC is used. The decreasing ordinary filtrations are cofinal,so quotient inverse limits and unions of prescribed linear-cutoff functors agree over ALL Q-algebras. This is not equality of same-index ideals,finite generation,stabilization,or equivalence of separate eventuality with linear safety.",
